    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d324">

                <pb facs="0408" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–444</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of
                            State to President Roosevelt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-04">April 4, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I enclose for your information and consideration a copy of a letter<anchor n="10"
                        xml:id="d324-f1"/> which I am forwarding to the Secretary of War commenting
                    upon a proposal by General Stilwell, concurred in by Ambassador Gauss, that you
                    send a message to the Generalissimo urging his assent to the dispatch
                    immediately of a military observers’ mission to the so-called Communist area in
                        China.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d324-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d324-f1" n="10" xml:id="d324-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d324-f2" n="11" xml:id="d324-f2-content">
                <p>President Roosevelt indicated his approval and on April 5 returned to the
                    Secretary of State the initialed copy of his letter to the Secretary of War.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
